.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-captcha-verify 1  "rev-stealth-captcha-verify " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-captcha\-verify \- Verify a previously\-issued token (round\-trips through the challenge provider\*(Aqs verify endpoint)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth captcha verify\fR <\fB\-\-type\fR> <\fB\-\-token\fR> <\fB\-\-secret\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify a CAPTCHA token by calling the challenge provider\*(Aqs server\-side verify endpoint. Returns the provider\*(Aqs structured verdict; the exit code reflects RPC outcome only (not the verdict itself).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR
Challenge type, same vocabulary as `solve \-\-type`
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Token returned by `solve`
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\fR \fI<SECRET>\fR
Provider secret (loaded from env in production)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBREV_STEALTH_CAPTCHA_SECRET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth captcha verify \-\-type recaptcha\-v2 \-\-token <TOKEN>
  $ rev\-stealth captcha verify \-\-type hcaptcha \-\-token <TOKEN> \-\-secret <SECRET>
  $ REV_STEALTH_CAPTCHA_SECRET=... rev\-stealth captcha verify \-\-type turnstile \-\-token <TOKEN>

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Verify RPC completed (read verdict from output).
  1  UserError        Bad args (unknown \-\-type, missing \-\-secret).
  2  TransientError   Provider network/timeout (retryable).
  3  PermanentError   Provider permanently rejected (unsupported type, bad config).

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_CAPTCHA_SECRET  Provider secret. Preferred over `\-\-secret` for ops use.
